\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\deftab1195\f0\fs24\cf0
\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The room was full of subtleties which could not be captured in a painting. The cool, dark grays called for a shade of blue which he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d never been able to find, or mix. The blackwood floor creaked under his step, and that slight toe-pressure, that tactile sense of something old expiring in the humidity, that could only be hinted at. Two windows set into the long wall sent breakfast sunbeams slanting across the sturdy dining table, and that light was alive with motes of dust fleeing from his breath\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 impossible to paint the feeling of having caused a stir. Then there was the ceiling, which sagged and cracked, as though the plastered clay had given up. The sense of dread that sag elicited could only be felt if one was standing underneath it and looking up.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re late,\u8221\'94 Vigram said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram sat at the head of the table, fat hands folded over his belly beard.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Sorry,\u8221\'94 Mandri replied as he unshouldered his satchel and set it down on the floor by the doorway. \u8220\'93The walk was little farther than I expected. And I didn\u8217\'92t\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram raised a patient hand. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s for the best,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93I should mention that we\u8217\'92re waiting on a third.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Who?\u8221\'94 Mandri asked}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93She prefers to introduce herself. I expect she\u8217\'92ll be here shortly. In the meantime, I crave your indulgence at my table; a meal is being prepared.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri quirked his head. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 am}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  hungry.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram smiled. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Do you like leech?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri blunted his immediate grimace with a thoughtful look. He didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t want Vigram to think him ungrateful, even if he was. \u8220\'93I will eat whatever you\u8217\'92re offering,\u8221\'94 he said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram nodded, then patted a spot at the table next to him.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri walked through the morning rays and took the seat. Once tucked into the table, he was reminded of how much bigger Vigram was. It had been a week since the initial invite, and he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d forgotten that the man was huge, tall and burly. He did remember Vigram\u8217\'92s broad face, his bald head and dark, tufted brows. Fifty-ish years of age. But that sense of a biding power, that sort of old-man strength, all that was an uncomfortable memory he\u8217\'92d tried to shed. Made him feel less about himself. And up close, the tightness of Vigram\u8217\'92s skin felt unnatural, like the man\u8217\'92s thick skull was about to burst right out of it. It made him hard to read. A polite, half-hearted smile was tucked inside his beard, but was it sincere? Probably not. The man was rich, and it was dangerous to think a rich man could be sincere.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri sat up straight. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Happy to finally be here,\u8221\'94 he said, trying to sound amenable.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes,\u8221\'94 Vigram said as he folded his hands back over his belly. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ve been looking forward to this as well. But, you should temper your expectations. I\u8217\'92m a difficult student. I get frustrated easily. I\u8217\'92ve been through, I would say, more than ten young painters like yourself.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93More than ten?\u8221\'94 Mandri asked.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You may have more success,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, \u8220\'93but know that this is unlikely.\u8221\'94 He shifted back in his seat so that he could lean forward and stick his elbows on the table. \u8220\'93You see, I am difficult to get along with. I require a }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 very}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  specific type of person. Someone who fits me like a glove, as they say.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll try my best.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram shook his head. His great beard sort of rippled and dusted the edge of the table. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t want your best,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93I want you to be comfortable. I should say, the faster we put away the masks we\u8217\'92re wearing and overcome this awkward discomfort of being strangers to each other, the better.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well, to be honest, I\u8217\'92ve sort of be been fearing this. I have heard that you\u8217\'92re, you know\u8230\'85difficult.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Ooooh?\u8221\'94 Vigram said, suddenly intrigued. \u8220\'93Let\u8217\'92s hear it. What have the prattling horde been saying about me?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I mean, you yourself said that you\u8217\'92ve run through a few instructors.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes? And?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Look, nothing bad was said, just, enough to suggest that your lack of progress does not lie with the quality of the instruction.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes, I already know. I get frustrated easily.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Right. And knowing that, I\u8217\'92m left wondering why you want to learn how to paint. I mean, if you don\u8217\'92t enjoy it, then why bother? A lot of people fall in love with the idea of painting pretty pictures, but not so much the process. The process is difficult, and depressing at points. You have to be very motivated.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What difficulties did }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 you }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 have to go through?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Plenty. Believe me.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But I am familiar with you and your work. At the age of ten you could paint a portrait in oil which rivaled the old Jeketian masters.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re overselling me.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nonsense. I watched you paint once, some years ago. A demonstration. I was part of a crowd. I watched you lay a single slap of umber down to define a woman\u8217\'92s chestnut skin, her high-arched cheek, the skull underneath, the light, the shadow, even the mood of the piece. One single stroke! Warms and cools in one single stroke. With twenty-four, you found a vivid likeness. There were a few extra nibbles to make the beauty\u8217\'92s eyes glisten and her cleavage heave, but nobody counted those. Well, I counted them. Lascivious men counted them. Every man counted them. Some women, presumably.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That skill,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, \u8220\'93Was the culmination of great amount effort.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93By the age of ten!?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I wouldn\u8217\'92t have been anywhere near ten if you were watching a demonstration. Besides, I wasn\u8217\'92t ever that good.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But you were!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93If I was, I wouldn\u8217\'92t be here, I don\u8217\'92t think. No offense.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You are here because you have degenerated. That\u8217\'92s why. That\u8217\'92s why I\u8217\'92m here, too. I should say, that\u8217\'92s why I want to learn how to paint. Mandri, we live in a degenerate culture.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri crinkled his nose. If he weren\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t careful, he might start an argument. Vigram was too wealthy. Mandri didn\u8217\'92t know the man well, but he it was clear enough already that the man would not permit disagreement. And Vigram wasn\u8217\'92t some skinny person with a scholar\u8217\'92s neck, one of those people with a mind so deep that they forget to eat and so you could be sure that they have interesting things to say. Vigram had probably never missed a meal in his life.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93My whole project,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, \u8220\'93is to push back against degeneracy. Art is the heat which raises a culture up. A purer expression of art is our route back to civilization.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You want your art to change the world?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why not?\u8221\'94 Vigram said. \u8220\'93Someone has to do it. It\u8217\'92s the only way. The problem runs that deep. Think of it\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the minds in our culture are so polluted that words have come to mean different things to different people.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What does the word, \u8216\'91white\u8217\'92 mean to you?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The color, white?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s good you should say that,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. \u8220\'93Yes, \u8216\'91white\u8217\'92 means the pure color \u8216\'91white\u8217\'92. Any and all variation in that meaning is a sign of degeneracy. Believe it or not, some people use the word white to refer to some other substance. In the far north, they call snow, \u8216\'91white\u8217\'92. But there\u8217\'92s a deeper problem\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 there\u8217\'92s the matter of the }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 feeling}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  one has when relating to the word, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91white\u8217\'92. The }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 meaning}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  of the word in that sense, what it }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 means}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  to}{\f1\fs24\b0\i1  }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 you as an individual. In this respect, there is a great difference of opinion, and that difference condemns this world.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m sorry, I don\u8217\'92t follow.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93When a Solitant priest hears the word \u8216\'91white\u8217\'92, he dreams of the pure white glow of Solraheen. Hrkan folk hear \u8216\'91white\u8217\'92 and think of the plain and stainless robes of Hrkan Lordship. Outland pokes hear \u8216\'91white\u8217\'92 and they dream of daggering down those plain and stainless robes. As it is with white, so it is with words, they mean different things to different people.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Is that bad?\u8221\'94 Mandri asked. \u8220\'93Differences of opinion seem inevitable.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I see you\u8217\'92ve been listening to the Solitants,\u8221\'94 Vigram said bitterly. \u8220\'93I should say, you have the stink of Solitant degeneracy about you. What\u8217\'92s that sermon called? \u8216\'91Art as exegetical instrument\u8217\'92? The one which wonders why Solraheen would choose to use such an equivocal thing as a word to create the world. How He dwelt in the void, spoke the sacred Word, the world emerged, and why people haven\u8217\'92t stopped arguing about the meaning of it all ever since. Solraheen chose to create the world out of wordstuff because He wanted to play with what He meant. He wanted }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 us}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  to play with it. But I say: this is false. Words are fixed. Back when Solraheen walked the earth, an artwork was nothing less than a divine message given physical form. Then evil entered the world, twisted the tongues of men, and now the heresy of art as a means of personal expression pollutes the minds of many. No! True art is a divine message. All else is degeneracy.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri rested his chin in his hand. He forced a pleasant smile. He hadn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t eaten in two days. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He thought to curse whoever invented table manners. Because what was the point of waiting for the host to take the first bite? People said it was selfish to not wait, but who was the selfish one? Was it the person who says, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m not going to wait for you,\u8221\'94 or the person who says, \u8220\'93How dare you not wait for me\u8221\'94? So long as everyone was sitting at the table, it was better to just eat. Feelings shouldn\u8217\'92t come into it.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What is art?\u8221\'94 Vigram asked. He was using his hands to communicate now, as if subjecting Mandri to a kind of surgery where the degeneracy of this fallen world was to be extracted from the mind by means of interrogation.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I say again, What is art? Who is an artist? Who isn\u8217\'92t? A painter, a sculptor, these are artists, yes, that\u8217\'92s reasonable to say, but what about a tax collector? Is he an artist too if he plumbs the depths of greed? Is a sheep-shearer plying her shears an artist if she\u8217\'92s sufficiently clever about it? What about a farmer? Give a young man a shovel, a field of dirt, friends to impress, and what does he do?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93He\u8217\'92d dig a penis,\u8221\'94 Mandri said absently. But Vigram\u8217\'92s eyes alighted}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes! That\u8217\'92s it exactly! The average Jandri boy would find it funny to dig a big old ugly in the dirt. He laughs because it doubles as a drainage ditch, just like the real thing. And to place such degeneracy in the same category as the cloud of colored windows which open up the ceiling of the Gambagall\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 well! }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 That}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  is an affront to the sacred! So you see, the Solitants are wrong, because if everyone is an artist, then the word is as useful as an unmarked weight.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram clutched his bearded jaw and winced. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I have a troublesome tooth,\u8221\'94 he said. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri saw how not accommodate his troublesome tooth. None of the food here did. This was Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s leech farm, and so every dish\u8217\'92s principal ingredient was some variation of the Meskalimi leech. This particular leech was a prized delicacy throughout the Hrkan world, as the meat, if it can be called meat, was quite sweet. It was also said to cure infertility, and somehow, fertility as well. It was also chewy. Each bite forced Vigram\u8217\'92s tongue into acrobatics. Two bites in, his tongue slipped, and the pain had him talking out the side of his cheek in an odd drawl. It hurt to hear the man speak, in more ways than one.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why not choose a different word?\u8221\'94 Mandri suggested as he dug into a bowl of mush. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Because words must have walls,\u8221\'94 Vigram said as he pushed his own plate away. \u8220\'93The true artist, I say this, the true artist is a divine instrument. They must be kept apart from the self-skinny horde.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri chowed down on the cold, crumbled chunks of what he supposed was boiled leech. It was quite bitter on account of the overpowering sauce, but the effort to suppress a gag helped keep him from speaking his mind.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You know,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, getting excited, \u8220\'93the Old Jandri word for \u8216\'91artist\u8217\'92 is lost to time, but there is a word in what\u8217\'92s left of that language fit for the task\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8216\'91bursheg\u8217\'92. It means something like \u8216\'91fertile ground\u8217\'92, but in the Solitant tradition it means \u8216\'91true artist\u8217\'92.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Interesting,\u8221\'94 Mandri lied.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll tell you what\u8217\'92s interesting,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, lifting his thick brows. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ve heard someone say that art has nothing to do with what a person makes. Have you ever heard that? I didn\u8217\'92t understand it at first, but you know, it\u8217\'92s true. True artistry, consider this, true artistry is a state of mind. Some of the greatest artists never made anything at all.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri stuffed his mouth with a breadroll in a futile attempt to stifle himself. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I was under the impression,\u8221\'94 he said as he worked the roll into his cheek, \u8220\'93that an artist makes art. I mean, that seems like the most straightforward definition to me. I mean, if we\u8217\'92re getting upset about people twisting words, then\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram frowned and tutted. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nobody makes anything,\u8221\'94 he insisted. \u8220\'93We can only ever rearrange. When you paint, you push pigment around. How is that any different than my footprints rearranging sand? No, either everyone is an artist, or, and this is my claim, an artist is a certain type}{\f1\fs24\b0\i1  }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 of}{\f1\fs24\b0\i1  }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 person. A certain type of }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 mind}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 . You know, too many big ideas, too many shallow excuses, that sort of thing. It\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s a mind marked by excess\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 not abundance\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 excess}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 .\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t look at me,\u8221\'94 Mandri said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram smiled. The fat swerve of his bottom lip was a baited hook. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So exaggerated is the artist\u8217\'92s sense of self that it becomes impossible to describe them without resorting to sarcasm.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re still looking at me.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s smile swerved. \u8220\'93There is no one else here.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Two slaves stood at attention by the kitchen\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s double-swing doors. Vigram\u8217\'92s blindness to their existence was cruel, but this did not dismantle his point.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram, you don\u8217\'92t know me.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He stabbed a thin strip of leech with his fork and tried to pinpoint the exact moment when he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d fallen out of life.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri bit down on the leech and chewed. He chewed and chewed. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 His biggest regret was when he stood in front of a good friend\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s painting of a sea storm, and he said, \u8220\'93This piece really }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 moves}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  me,\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 and then he made a show of walking away. It was funny. People laughed. All must bear witness to his mop of black hair as it flounced itself in time with his skinny, stiff-backed step. \u8220\'93I weep at every stroke,\u8221\'94 he said as he flashed a knowing smile.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Back in those days, he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d say these kinds of things directly to a fellow artist\u8217\'92s face if he could get to it. He didn\u8217\'92t think of it as bullying because artists, like himself, were safe targets for playful derision\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 it wasn\u8217\'92t the person he was making fun of, it was their failed attempts to express themselves, and those were }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 completely}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  different things. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d never go after the person.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 No, never.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Artists were the best people. They needed tough skin, unearned confidence, and a flair for the dramatic. Without any of that, they die unremembered. Then there is the servility. Above all, an artist must be servile to the hand that feeds, and look at that, Vigram had a lot of food at his table. And here he was, eating it.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d become the one thing he\u8217\'92d swore he\u8217\'92d never be.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 An employee.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 This needed to be rectified.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He looked to Vigram, who had been babbling about artistry in the \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91classical sense\u8217\'92, as could only be found in the \u8216\'91uncorrupted ages\u8217\'92.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram,\u8221\'94 Mandri said confidently, \u8220\'93you are an idiot.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram choked on a wad of smushed leech. He coughed, pounded his chest, then coughed again. Once recovered, he glared at Mandri with his protuberant eyes, oblivious to the brown specks of food in his long beard. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93In whose house do we sit?!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yours.\u8221\'94 Mandri said as he mustered a disarming smile. \u8220\'93But when it comes to these things, when it comes to matters of art, I am correct. If I am not correct, then you certainly aren\u8217\'92t.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why? Because I like some painters who aren\u8217\'92t you?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t paint anymore, so I don\u8217\'92t care who you like.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93If you\u8217\'92re not a painter, then why do I pay you for lessons?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93These lessons are a charity.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri, I }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 pay}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  you!\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Even so.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Leech juice dripped down the corner of Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s lip, accenting his frown. He wiped it away, then broke into a jolly smile. \u8220\'93Hah!\u8221\'94 he chortled as he stabbed his clam shell into a bowl of fermented leech. So much lard was mushed into those leeches that the gray paste could grease a wheel. Vigram\u8217\'92s outstretched tongue batted at the stringy slop before he slumped it all down his gullet. He patted his fat lips dry with his fifth napkin, then threw it onto the floor to join the others.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We both know,\u8221\'94 he said, \u8220\'93that you only come here for the money.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Then we are both mistaken.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram rolled his eyes and set his leech lard mush aside. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Listen,\u8221\'94 he said. He put on his business face, which looked something like a spooked frog. \u8220\'93You have a gift. I should say that I believe in your talent. You should believe me when I say that success is there for the taking. I know you don\u8217\'92t want to debase yourself by doing what it takes to succeed, but the money is easy. It is }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 sitting}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  there for the taking. People }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 want}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  to give it to you. A young man such as you, I cannot understand why you won\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t even try. Do you not want a woman on your arm? A house? Respect?\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri settled into his chair because he knew what was coming next: Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s life story. It always came out as a sort of instructional.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The first step in the accumulation of wealth was often left out because not everyone could easily murder their father to inherit a sizable sum. That being said, four ounces of silver would do.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Next, loan those four ounces out to a leech farm. Why a leech farm? Beyond the blunt symbolism of the leech, there\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s not much of a reason. It is important to remember that not every leech farm is the same. Look for a farm that supplies a Solitant temple with leeches for their bloodletting rituals. That\u8217\'92s a surefire bet because temples are always the last thing the mob will torch in lean times. When the lean times hit especially hard, when the only bread available is made from fern-roots, the leech farm will feel the squeeze. They\u8217\'92ll ask for leniency on the interest rate. Do not budge. Take over the farm. The leechmen might accuse you of committing usury against Solraheen Himself, because in some small way you are, but Solraheen is dead and so what does it matter? Get together with a priest and pray about it around a jug of beer, flash him a slip of silver, and the bleary shine will blind him to all the world\u8217\'92s iniquity.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 With the farm in hand, begin to lend smaller amounts over shorter terms to farmers who need emergency loans to pay their taxes after droughts or infestations. Split these debts up and sell them off in Meskalim\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s bond market. There\u8217\'92s not much money in Meskalim itself, but it has a busy port and that means access to all the important markets of the Hrkan world.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 From there, it\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s a simple matter of reducing your eyes to tiny pinpricks, ridding yourself of limbs, segmenting the body, and now that you\u8217\'92ve transformed into a leech, you may attach firmly to the continent\u8217\'92s rump and drink your fill. Anyone who tries to shake you off before you\u8217\'92ve finished becomes your slave. You pick out the salvageable fools for your own use, and now you\u8217\'92ve got a brood of leeches pouring over lists of sums credited and debts owed. So long as you maintain a layer of abstraction between these creatures and your henchmen, it\u8217\'92s all self-sustaining.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 And that\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s it.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Now you have a comfortable life.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Idle hours.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No debasement necessary,\u8221\'94 Vigram added before licking his}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1  plump fingers clean of sun-dried leech oil. This oil was a true delicacy, squeezed as it was from the salivary glands of leeches aged twenty years or more. Leeches that big are more devourers than bloodsuckers, so they\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92re much more expensive to feed.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Now,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. \u8220\'93}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 You know all about the making of a painting. That\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s why I respect you. I know all about the making of money. At a certain point you have to join them up, because the world doesn\u8217\'92t work how it should. The world works how it works. You }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 have}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  to make a living.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Do I?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Boy! Where is your ambition? Do you even have a Spark? Sol\u8217\'92s light, I\u8217\'92m making this as easy as possible. I know you are here for the money, so you must have }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 some}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  ambition. Why not have more?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Again, Vigram, I\u8217\'92m not here for the money.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Then why walk all this way?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Because.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93}{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 Because?}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t need a reason to do whatever it is that I do. I just do it. I\u8217\'92m here. That\u8217\'92s all.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram stared at Mandri with a slack jaw. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re a very confused boy,\u8221\'94 he said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yeah, well, I\u8217\'92m here.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So you are.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 With that, Vigram clapped his meaty hands, prompting one of the nameless slaves to come and take his plates. Once done, he stood up. His chair protested the sudden shift of his massive weight with a terrible squeak.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We will begin,\u8221\'94 he said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri nodded, then wiped his own mouth and excused himself from the table. He took his time, because he wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t looking forward to beginning anything. But, he had to. He needed the money. He needed it quite badly. He just didn\u8217\'92t want to tell Vigram what it was for, or else the man might try to intervene.}}